1
00:00:19,652 --> 00:00:21,357
Seibei Iguchi
Hiroyuki Sanada

2
00:00:24,991 --> 00:00:26,491
Tomoe
Rie Miyazawa

3
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,570
Directed by
Yoji Yamada

4
00:01:26,953 --> 00:01:28,453
Not that way

5
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,927
No, no, no!

6
00:01:43,236 --> 00:01:44,736
Thank you. You may go

7
00:02:00,153 --> 00:02:02,388
After a long illness
my mother died...

8
00:02:04,524 --> 00:02:06,024
...when I was five

9
00:02:08,027 --> 00:02:09,527
She had consumption...

10
00:02:11,998 --> 00:02:15,292
...so from when I can remember
I wasn't allowed near her

11
00:02:17,437 --> 00:02:19,848
Thus I have almost no memory
of my mother

12
00:02:31,251 --> 00:02:32,751
Ito...Ito...

13
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:35,987
You poor little darling!

14
00:02:59,779 --> 00:03:03,896
I am from Unasaka, in the northeast
in what is now Yamagata Prefecture

15
00:03:06,953 --> 00:03:10,305
Before 1868 it was the castle town
of the Unasaka clan...

16
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:13,120
...a small fief of 70,000 koku
of rice per year

17
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:39,784
Well done, one and all

18
00:03:41,654 --> 00:03:43,154
That's it for today

19
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,630
Sakaguchi...

20
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:56,744
I've heard there's a good
drinking place in Hakkenmachi...

21
00:03:58,605 --> 00:04:00,105
Oh, you mean 'Hisago'?

22
00:04:01,274 --> 00:04:02,559
Feel like a drink?

23
00:04:02,609 --> 00:04:04,109
A fine idea

24
00:04:05,211 --> 00:04:06,711
Kawanami, will you come?

25
00:04:08,147 --> 00:04:09,566
I will

26
00:04:09,616 --> 00:04:11,116
Iguchi?

27
00:04:11,851 --> 00:04:13,351
For a change?

28
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:15,854
Not me, thanks

29
00:04:16,022 --> 00:04:17,522
We can't twist your arm?

30
00:04:17,991 --> 00:04:19,491
lf you'll excuse me...

31
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:25,763
Twilight's not very exciting
is he

32
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:41,786
With a sick wife, two young daughters
and an aged mother in his care...

33
00:04:43,016 --> 00:04:46,074
...my father was unable
to drink with his colleagues

34
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,390
He had to hurry home
every evening at dusk

35
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,253
I was told the men
he worked with...

36
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:11,474
...gave him the cruel nickname
of 'Twilight Seibei'

37
00:05:16,182 --> 00:05:17,682
THE TWILIGHT SAMURAI

38
00:05:36,636 --> 00:05:37,987
Ito...

39
00:05:38,037 --> 00:05:39,537
Father!

40
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:41,606
Up you go!

41
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,180
Your face is dirty

42
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,333
Father's back!

43
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:10,235
Welcome home

44
00:06:16,309 --> 00:06:18,014
Codfish stew tonight, Kayano?

45
00:06:23,015 --> 00:06:24,515
Don't drop it

46
00:06:27,019 --> 00:06:29,489
I'm home, Mother
How are you this evening?

47
00:06:32,258 --> 00:06:34,081
Of what household are you, sir?

48
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:39,513
I am Seibei Iguchi of the
Unasaka CIan, Castle Stores

49
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,400
I see...

50
00:06:45,271 --> 00:06:48,506
She's getting worse. She doesn't
even know her own son!

51
00:06:59,952 --> 00:07:02,599
Kayano, I've simmered
some burdock. Take some

52
00:07:04,023 --> 00:07:06,846
Thank you. You're always
so kind to my daughters

53
00:07:08,127 --> 00:07:09,715
Naota...you can go home now

54
00:07:12,131 --> 00:07:13,631
Yup

55
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:29,480
Good evening

56
00:07:31,551 --> 00:07:34,433
But Yazaki, can't we do something
about Twilight?

57
00:07:36,389 --> 00:07:39,447
His kimono's all ripped
and hardly ever takes a bath

58
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,248
There's this smell
when you get close to him

59
00:07:44,564 --> 00:07:46,064
lt just won't do!

60
00:07:47,266 --> 00:07:49,913
Yes, sir. We all find it
very hard to stomach

61
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:53,611
We've asked around about
finding him a new wife...

62
00:07:53,873 --> 00:07:56,225
...but no woman would want
his situation

63
00:07:57,577 --> 00:07:59,077
lndeed!

64
00:07:59,412 --> 00:08:02,098
He's got two young girls
a senile old mother...

65
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:04,265
...and 20 of his 50koku
gone in debt

66
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:10,177
Any woman who went to him
would have to take in work

67
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:14,134
Yes, he owes money
all over the place

68
00:08:15,094 --> 00:08:17,858
I don't know how he paid for
his wife's funeral

69
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:22,419
Not even selling your sword
would pay for a funeral like that

70
00:08:24,704 --> 00:08:27,256
A funeral! That's something
I have to worry about, too

71
00:08:27,306 --> 00:08:29,717
My father's not going to
last much longer

72
00:08:32,144 --> 00:08:35,026
Kawanami's lucky
Young parents and a pretty wife!

73
00:08:37,550 --> 00:08:40,667
You'd better go easy with her
lt could hurt your work

74
00:08:42,455 --> 00:08:45,337
ls that why you're always
cat-napping on the job?

75
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:49,193
I am not!

76
00:08:49,762 --> 00:08:51,262
Listen to him!

77
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:53,197
Kumi...

78
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,866
Welcome!

79
00:08:54,934 --> 00:08:56,434
lsn't she gorgeous!

80
00:08:57,336 --> 00:08:58,836
Kume...

81
00:09:24,263 --> 00:09:25,763
Bed-time, Gran

82
00:09:28,501 --> 00:09:30,001
Good night, Seibei

83
00:09:31,370 --> 00:09:32,870
Good night

84
00:09:35,608 --> 00:09:37,431
lt looks like
she remembered me

85
00:09:40,713 --> 00:09:44,065
The Master said: To rule a land
of a thousand chariots---

86
00:09:47,219 --> 00:09:48,719
Kayano...

87
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:52,476
That's Confucius, isn't it?
When did you start learning that?

88
00:09:53,659 --> 00:09:56,247
At the end of last month
The teacher says...

89
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:00,912
...from now on even girls
will need book learning

90
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,000
That's good

91
00:10:03,736 --> 00:10:06,853
When I was a boy I read Confucius
over and over again

92
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:13,945
Father...

93
00:10:14,914 --> 00:10:16,678
lf I learn to do
needlework...

94
00:10:17,249 --> 00:10:18,954
...someday I can make kimonos

95
00:10:24,557 --> 00:10:27,145
But what good will
book learning ever do me?

96
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:33,364
Well, it probably won't ever be
as useful as needlework

97
00:10:43,542 --> 00:10:45,042
But you know...

98
00:10:46,012 --> 00:10:48,306
...book learning gives you
the power...

99
00:10:52,018 --> 00:10:53,518
...to think

100
00:10:55,021 --> 00:10:58,785
However the world might change
if you have the power to think...

101
00:11:01,093 --> 00:11:02,975
...you'll always survive somehow

102
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:06,330
That's true for boys
and for girls

103
00:11:10,069 --> 00:11:11,487
All right?

104
00:11:11,537 --> 00:11:13,037
Yes

105
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,340
Keep reading, then

106
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:20,088
Tseng Tzu said: Each day
in three ways---

107
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:24,315
...I ask myself---

108
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:29,459
...if I have faithfully carried out
what I undertook for another---

109
00:11:30,723 --> 00:11:33,723
My mother's illness had left
my father deep in debt

110
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:39,054
As Grandmother lost her wits, all the
housework, the gathering of fuel...

111
00:11:40,332 --> 00:11:42,273
...and the field work fell to him

112
00:11:45,404 --> 00:11:48,051
Left with little time
to attend to himself...

113
00:11:49,742 --> 00:11:52,094
...he gradually became
unkempt and grimy

114
00:11:55,614 --> 00:11:58,143
As his daughter, I felt terrible
about this

115
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:05,389
Wipe off that dust!

116
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:09,360
They're coming!

117
00:12:11,997 --> 00:12:13,497
His Lordship attends!

118
00:12:14,467 --> 00:12:15,967
Kawanami! Quick!

119
00:12:17,603 --> 00:12:19,103
Provisions'

120
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:24,180
Vital stores of food for when
the clan must fight, or the castle...

121
00:12:26,612 --> 00:12:28,112
...is besieged

122
00:12:29,215 --> 00:12:31,273
Next we have the Salt Storehouse...

123
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:39,794
Here you have your beans
green, soy and red...

124
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:44,725
We pay particular attention
to keeping them dry

125
00:12:46,732 --> 00:12:50,084
Dried giant horse-radish
dried fiddleheads, miso paste...

126
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:52,436
Kusaka!

127
00:12:55,975 --> 00:12:57,475
This is dried codfish...

128
00:12:59,478 --> 00:13:02,183
...very important provisioning
in times of war

129
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,116
How much have we got?

130
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:08,419
Iguchi...

131
00:13:13,225 --> 00:13:15,107
Iguchi'? You may answer
directly

132
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,916
By your leave. We have
760 strips...

133
00:13:24,904 --> 00:13:26,904
...by weight approximately
120 kan

134
00:13:28,107 --> 00:13:29,607
How long does it keep?

135
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:33,039
Between five and ten years

136
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,162
This here is the oldest
we have.

137
00:13:37,516 --> 00:13:39,221
lt was acquired
six years ago

138
00:13:41,053 --> 00:13:45,053
This dried cod from Kansaki is best
lt holds its taste for ten years

139
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:54,125
That strange smell I noticed
is it you?

140
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:04,634
CIan retainers must serve
as examples to the common folk

141
00:14:07,112 --> 00:14:08,612
Keep yourself clean

142
00:14:10,049 --> 00:14:11,549
Yes, Milord!

143
00:14:13,485 --> 00:14:14,985
Carry on

144
00:14:19,458 --> 00:14:20,958
ldiot!

145
00:14:31,604 --> 00:14:33,104
Sir, I...

146
00:14:33,305 --> 00:14:34,805
I'll speak to you later

147
00:14:35,574 --> 00:14:36,325
But...

148
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:37,875
Be quiet!

149
00:14:42,648 --> 00:14:44,148
Iguchi!

150
00:14:46,118 --> 00:14:47,618
You damn fool!

151
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:54,526
The story spread
throughout the castle

152
00:14:56,862 --> 00:14:58,744
My father became
a laughingstock

153
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:12,476
My Great-Uncle came from
the main house in a foul humor

154
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:22,720
Hello!

155
00:15:23,222 --> 00:15:24,722
Hello!

156
00:15:26,992 --> 00:15:28,492
Seibei!

157
00:15:29,561 --> 00:15:31,061
lt's Uncle...

158
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:34,265
I'm in for it now

159
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:38,179
ls anybody here?
What, are you all dead?!

160
00:15:40,239 --> 00:15:41,739
Coming!

161
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,442
Kayano, make some tea

162
00:15:45,311 --> 00:15:46,328
Who is it?

163
00:15:46,378 --> 00:15:47,878
Great-Uncle!

164
00:15:49,515 --> 00:15:51,015
Disgraceful!

165
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:57,935
You appeared before His Lordship
unbathed, smelling like dried cod

166
00:15:58,123 --> 00:15:59,475
The unpleasant impression
you created...

167
00:15:59,525 --> 00:16:01,230
...shames the house of Iguchi

168
00:16:04,930 --> 00:16:06,430
That was inexcusable

169
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:11,152
I went to Senior Retainer Terauchi
and apologized for you

170
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:18,075
His Lordship is a generous man
so he did not find fault

171
00:16:19,778 --> 00:16:21,836
Had that been his father, though...

172
00:16:23,582 --> 00:16:25,640
...this would have meant
hara-kiri!

173
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:28,523
I never dreamed
it would cause so much trouble

174
00:16:30,022 --> 00:16:31,522
I beg your forgiveness

175
00:16:33,258 --> 00:16:34,758
Kayano?

176
00:16:36,395 --> 00:16:37,895
How old are you now?

177
00:16:38,630 --> 00:16:40,130
I am ten years old

178
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:43,249
Are you working at
your lessons?

179
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:47,947
I'm learning needlework
and Confucius

180
00:16:49,241 --> 00:16:51,241
A girl has no need
of the classics

181
00:16:53,245 --> 00:16:55,539
All you need is
to write women's script

182
00:16:56,548 --> 00:16:59,335
Too much book learning
and you'll never be a bride

183
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:00,885
You can go

184
00:17:09,995 --> 00:17:12,230
I am here today
on an important matter

185
00:17:16,969 --> 00:17:18,469
A marriage arrangement

186
00:17:19,671 --> 00:17:23,200
You need a hard-working wife
to escape the misery you are in

187
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:29,348
A village-headman acquaintance
has an unmarried daughter...

188
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:32,323
...whom he agrees
to marry to you

189
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:38,461
He knows you are poor, have two
young daughters and a senile mother

190
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:43,882
I'm sure you realize that you are
in no position to demand beauty

191
00:17:44,463 --> 00:17:47,874
You need a healthy wife with
big haunches to bear children

192
00:17:49,201 --> 00:17:50,701
Her face is of no concern

193
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:54,967
So I'll proceed with this
if you don't mind

194
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,980
With all due respect
I must differ

195
00:18:05,784 --> 00:18:07,284
How?

196
00:18:07,553 --> 00:18:10,964
I am not nearly as miserable
in my living as you may think

197
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:17,817
Of course, offending His Lordship
by appearing unbathed before him...

198
00:18:18,163 --> 00:18:20,633
...was wrong, and I vow
never to repeat it

199
00:18:24,736 --> 00:18:26,236
However...

200
00:18:27,039 --> 00:18:30,215
...watching my daughters
as they grow day by day is...

201
00:18:33,045 --> 00:18:34,545
...how shall I put it?

202
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:39,633
lt's like watching crops ripen
or flowers grow in a field

203
00:18:44,823 --> 00:18:46,323
I enjoy it very much

204
00:18:49,895 --> 00:18:52,542
I'm not sure if the lady
of whom you speak...

205
00:18:53,332 --> 00:18:54,832
...would understand that

206
00:18:57,903 --> 00:19:00,197
Who would understand
such foolishness?!

207
00:19:03,575 --> 00:19:05,398
You've always been like this...

208
00:19:06,778 --> 00:19:10,307
...tormenting your poor father
with this prattling of yours!

209
00:19:12,584 --> 00:19:15,819
What has your marriage
got to do with crops in a field?

210
00:19:18,056 --> 00:19:20,291
Then I beg leave
to speak more clearly

211
00:19:21,793 --> 00:19:25,616
I ask that you not concern yourself
with questions of my marriage

212
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,144
You defy the main branch
of your family?!

213
00:19:31,470 --> 00:19:32,970
You are welcome here

214
00:19:36,141 --> 00:19:37,641
Kinu...are you well?

215
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,511
I am, thank you

216
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:43,648
May I ask of which household
you come?

217
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:49,186
I'm your damn brother!

218
00:19:49,588 --> 00:19:51,823
Take her away, Seibei
She's a nuisance

219
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:54,858
Mother...

220
00:19:55,394 --> 00:19:58,041
Most unseemly! What will
the neighbors think?

221
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:01,378
Tie her to a post somewhere!

222
00:20:06,371 --> 00:20:08,312
'Expect no more help from me!'...

223
00:20:13,011 --> 00:20:16,069
...shouted my great-uncle
as he left in high dudgeon

224
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:20,384
Can you do that?

225
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:23,287
Let me see

226
00:20:28,594 --> 00:20:30,476
Here...twist it
as you fit it in

227
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,200
ls Gran asleep?

228
00:20:36,435 --> 00:20:37,935
Yes

229
00:20:39,004 --> 00:20:40,504
Good

230
00:20:40,706 --> 00:20:42,206
Father...

231
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:44,575
Gran was crying, you know

232
00:20:46,545 --> 00:20:48,045
Uncle shouted at her

233
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:52,249
Poor Gran!

234
00:20:56,855 --> 00:20:58,355
Do you like Uncle?

235
00:21:01,293 --> 00:21:02,793
You don't?

236
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:08,499
I hate him

237
00:21:14,373 --> 00:21:17,549
He came to talk about a new wife
for me, but I said no

238
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:24,516
I don't want to take
any help from him

239
00:21:26,885 --> 00:21:28,826
You'd think we were
buying a cow!

240
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:33,769
All she needs is to be healthy
that's rude to the lady as well

241
00:21:40,098 --> 00:21:41,598
Are you two lonely...

242
00:21:44,636 --> 00:21:46,136
...without a mother?

243
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,346
I'm not lonely if you're here

244
00:21:52,644 --> 00:21:54,144
Me, too

245
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,651
That's my girls

246
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:13,335
Do you want the toilet, Gran?

247
00:22:41,727 --> 00:22:43,227
Look!

248
00:22:43,962 --> 00:22:46,079
Butterbur buds!
Get lots, all right?

249
00:22:52,604 --> 00:22:54,104
What's that?

250
00:22:56,475 --> 00:22:57,975
A child!

251
00:22:59,144 --> 00:23:01,438
The poor thing!
He's nothing but bones!

252
00:23:03,315 --> 00:23:04,815
Where'd he come from?

253
00:23:06,084 --> 00:23:07,584
Matsukawa, maybe

254
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:10,320
Rise to Buddha!

255
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:14,437
As children
we loved to go gathering herbs...

256
00:23:16,161 --> 00:23:17,984
...by the river
in early spring

257
00:23:21,199 --> 00:23:22,963
But those were times
of famine

258
00:23:25,637 --> 00:23:28,657
The cold meltwater often brought
the bodies of peasants...

259
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,207
...dead of starvation

260
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,415
Aim...

261
00:23:43,221 --> 00:23:44,721
Fire!

262
00:23:52,030 --> 00:23:53,530
All of you, watch me

263
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:55,499
EIbows up...

264
00:23:56,802 --> 00:23:58,302
Brace the right knee...

265
00:23:59,137 --> 00:24:01,078
Seibei! Sorry to keep you
waiting

266
00:24:05,343 --> 00:24:06,843
You went to Kyoto?

267
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:11,317
Yes, with the Majordomo to talk
to merchants there and in Osaka

268
00:24:11,516 --> 00:24:13,016
What's Kyoto like?

269
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:17,349
I had high hopes for it
but it was horrible

270
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:21,880
I've never seen the like
of Miyako-oji Boulevard

271
00:24:24,429 --> 00:24:28,252
Filthy masterless samurai from
all over the country everywhere...

272
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:31,694
...cursing and swearing
in dialects you can't understand

273
00:24:33,071 --> 00:24:36,835
Then someone shouts 'Divine
punishment!' and the swords come out

274
00:24:40,679 --> 00:24:44,149
The Kamo River's full of headless
corpses all swollen up...

275
00:24:47,853 --> 00:24:49,970
I thought it'd be geishas in Gion...

276
00:24:56,027 --> 00:24:57,527
Dear me!

277
00:25:00,365 --> 00:25:01,865
Prime!

278
00:25:03,068 --> 00:25:04,568
Aim!

279
00:25:05,537 --> 00:25:07,037
Fire!

280
00:25:08,106 --> 00:25:09,606
Misfire!

281
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:12,342
Wait! What's wrong?

282
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:16,298
Ow!

283
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,848
Fool!

284
00:25:18,850 --> 00:25:20,350
I told you to wait!

285
00:25:21,953 --> 00:25:23,453
They're a bit late

286
00:25:26,057 --> 00:25:28,468
The Choshu clan may have been
beaten once

287
00:25:28,827 --> 00:25:30,709
but they'll be back with Satsuma

288
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:35,578
They'll snuff out 250 years of
Shoguns like the wind does a candle

289
00:25:37,068 --> 00:25:38,568
What's our clan doing?

290
00:25:39,104 --> 00:25:40,751
Our leaders aren't thinking!

291
00:25:44,009 --> 00:25:46,009
How would you like
to go to Kyoto?

292
00:25:49,447 --> 00:25:51,741
The Emperor's palace
is short of guards

293
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:53,884
I'll recommend you

294
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:56,053
You'll see how things are

295
00:25:57,255 --> 00:26:00,843
Someone like you shouldn't be
stuck in a field here right now

296
00:26:02,093 --> 00:26:03,916
I'm afraid
you over-estimate me

297
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:08,398
The times are changing

298
00:26:10,502 --> 00:26:13,854
When they do, I'll give up
samurai status and be a farmer

299
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:19,271
That's what I'm suited for

300
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,449
You're a strange one

301
00:26:28,553 --> 00:26:30,053
But you always were

302
00:26:33,892 --> 00:26:35,392
No ambition at all

303
00:26:37,829 --> 00:26:39,329
Oh, I nearly forgot...

304
00:26:42,734 --> 00:26:44,734
My condolences
on your bereavement

305
00:26:49,007 --> 00:26:50,507
Burn a joss stick for her

306
00:26:51,443 --> 00:26:52,943
You didn't have to...

307
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:58,474
I wanted to send my sister
to the funeral in my place...

308
00:26:58,617 --> 00:27:01,322
...but she was having
some troubles of her own

309
00:27:03,021 --> 00:27:04,205
I'm sorry

310
00:27:04,255 --> 00:27:05,755
Miss Tomoe? What's wrong?

311
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:11,724
You know she married the son
of Captain Koda...

312
00:27:14,099 --> 00:27:16,628
lt turns out this Toyotaro
is a mean drunk.

313
00:27:18,903 --> 00:27:20,903
lf I'd known
I'd never have agreed

314
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:23,240
A mean drunk?

315
00:27:23,541 --> 00:27:25,041
He'd hit her, kick her...

316
00:27:27,278 --> 00:27:29,748
She'd come running
to my house to get away

317
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:33,551
I was worried
one day he'd kill her...

318
00:27:34,953 --> 00:27:37,600
...so I got the Castle
to order them divorced

319
00:27:38,690 --> 00:27:40,108
Divorced?

320
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,658
Just recently

321
00:27:42,293 --> 00:27:44,116
So now Tomoe's
back at my house

322
00:27:48,266 --> 00:27:49,766
Really?

323
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:57,543
And here I thought she was the wife
of a fine 1200-koku samurai

324
00:27:59,110 --> 00:28:00,610
I had no idea

325
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:05,849
I made a mistake. She's gone
through hell because of me

326
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,859
Well done, one and all

327
00:28:17,262 --> 00:28:18,762
That's it for today

328
00:28:27,472 --> 00:28:28,972
Sakaguchi...

329
00:28:29,808 --> 00:28:32,455
Sakaguchi! Feel like
dropping in at 'Hisago'?

330
00:28:33,912 --> 00:28:35,412
You want to see O-Kume!

331
00:28:35,914 --> 00:28:37,198
Quiet!

332
00:28:37,248 --> 00:28:38,748
You come too, Kawanami

333
00:28:39,017 --> 00:28:40,135
Again?

334
00:28:40,185 --> 00:28:41,169
Damn right!

335
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:42,719
I'll be going

336
00:28:43,321 --> 00:28:44,821
Iguchi...

337
00:28:45,523 --> 00:28:48,758
You should come see the girls
Take your mind off things

338
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:50,393
I'm fine, thanks.

339
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:55,483
Iguchi...

340
00:28:55,533 --> 00:28:57,033
Don't waste your breath

341
00:29:10,548 --> 00:29:12,430
Look, Naota. The azaleas are out

342
00:29:12,917 --> 00:29:14,417
Yup

343
00:29:23,661 --> 00:29:25,161
Kayano, Ito, I'm home!

344
00:29:29,067 --> 00:29:30,567
No one's here...

345
00:29:39,744 --> 00:29:41,244
Welcome home

346
00:29:45,850 --> 00:29:47,350
lt's been a long time

347
00:29:53,892 --> 00:29:55,392
Uh...perhaps there's...um

348
00:30:00,498 --> 00:30:02,262
You were out
when I came by...

349
00:30:08,706 --> 00:30:12,058
Have you forgotten me?
I'm Iinuma's younger sister, Tomoe

350
00:30:17,148 --> 00:30:18,648
Oh, Miss Tomoe!

351
00:30:21,619 --> 00:30:23,119
I didn't know you

352
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:28,970
I've just seen your brother today
He told me what had happened

353
00:30:31,629 --> 00:30:33,452
So you know all about it, then?

354
00:30:37,268 --> 00:30:38,768
Yes

355
00:30:39,704 --> 00:30:42,292
Because of that I'm back
living at his house

356
00:30:44,242 --> 00:30:47,300
There's nothing for me to do
so they have me weaving

357
00:30:48,446 --> 00:30:49,946
I came here to escape

358
00:30:52,150 --> 00:30:53,650
You're very welcome

359
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:56,519
Let's go inside

360
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:00,857
Your sock...

361
00:31:00,925 --> 00:31:02,425
Oh, yes...

362
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:16,273
lt seems your father
had forgotten me!

363
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:19,071
We always played together!

364
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:22,579
Welcome home

365
00:31:23,882 --> 00:31:26,470
Kayano, Ito, this is Miss Tomoe
We're, uh...

366
00:31:30,455 --> 00:31:33,043
Childhood friends
He always used to tease me

367
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,058
I did not!

368
00:31:35,827 --> 00:31:37,327
I got a present

369
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:39,562
Me, too

370
00:31:39,931 --> 00:31:41,431
Aren't they pretty!

371
00:31:43,434 --> 00:31:44,934
Mother, I'm home

372
00:31:45,470 --> 00:31:46,970
Welcome home

373
00:31:47,372 --> 00:31:48,872
Do you know this lady?

374
00:31:50,942 --> 00:31:52,824
She's Miss Tomoe
the Iinuma girl

375
00:31:53,144 --> 00:31:54,644
See? She remembered me

376
00:31:55,647 --> 00:31:58,823
That's good. And of course
you remember me, don't you?

377
00:32:02,921 --> 00:32:04,509
Of which household are you?

378
00:32:08,893 --> 00:32:10,393
I'm your son

379
00:32:12,163 --> 00:32:13,663
You are, are you?

380
00:32:14,165 --> 00:32:15,665
Hello

381
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:17,934
Tane, watch the hotpot

382
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:24,555
lt was as if our house was brighter
from the moment Miss Tomoe arrived

383
00:32:29,814 --> 00:32:32,343
I've never forgotten
lt was when I was five

384
00:32:32,417 --> 00:32:34,946
I always wanted to do
whatever the boys did

385
00:32:38,156 --> 00:32:41,273
Once I was climbing a pine tree
and a branch broke...

386
00:32:43,361 --> 00:32:44,861
...and I got hurt

387
00:32:45,196 --> 00:32:46,696
Really?

388
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:50,180
Yes! Your father happened
to be there that day...

389
00:32:51,035 --> 00:32:54,446
...and he carried me piggy-back
all the way to the doctor!

390
00:32:56,574 --> 00:32:58,074
I think he was 12 or 13

391
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:03,980
His back was this big!

392
00:33:06,951 --> 00:33:09,833
Just like a grown-up's
He made me feel so safe...

393
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:14,491
Do you remember, Seibei?

394
00:33:15,893 --> 00:33:17,834
I remember
something like that...

395
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:24,217
When I was nine
my mother told me...

396
00:33:25,203 --> 00:33:27,379
...I couldn't play
with boys any more

397
00:33:29,574 --> 00:33:31,074
I was so sad...

398
00:33:33,578 --> 00:33:35,283
Being a girl's no fun, Kayano

399
00:33:37,048 --> 00:33:38,548
Drip, drip drip...

400
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,607
...come our Chonbei's tears

401
00:33:44,622 --> 00:33:46,122
Drip, drip, drip...

402
00:33:46,758 --> 00:33:48,640
Let's catch his falling tears...

403
00:33:51,295 --> 00:33:52,795
...and wipe them away...

404
00:33:54,198 --> 00:33:55,698
Wipe them away...

405
00:33:57,301 --> 00:33:59,418
Let's take his
tear-soaked kimono...

406
00:34:01,939 --> 00:34:02,957
...and wash it clean...

407
00:34:03,007 --> 00:34:04,507
Wash it clean...

408
00:34:04,876 --> 00:34:07,052
Let's take the kimono
we've washed...

409
00:34:08,646 --> 00:34:10,146
...and wring it out...

410
00:34:10,581 --> 00:34:12,081
Wring it out...

411
00:34:12,617 --> 00:34:14,969
Let's take the kimono
we've wrung out...

412
00:34:16,687 --> 00:34:18,187
...and hang it to dry...

413
00:34:18,656 --> 00:34:20,156
Hang it to dry...

414
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:28,681
You haven't changed
at all, have you

415
00:34:32,003 --> 00:34:34,591
lt's as if I'm
a completely different person

416
00:34:38,443 --> 00:34:39,943
That's not true

417
00:34:41,612 --> 00:34:43,788
You still smile
just like you used to

418
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:51,242
You don't have to console me
I know I've changed

419
00:34:57,361 --> 00:35:00,066
People told me how radiant
a bride you were...

420
00:35:02,133 --> 00:35:04,133
...when you went to
the Koda house

421
00:35:05,269 --> 00:35:06,769
I don't want to remember

422
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:34,797
lt's very late
I'll leave you here

423
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:41,137
Say hello to your brother

424
00:35:44,742 --> 00:35:46,330
Your beard's growing out...

425
00:35:48,312 --> 00:35:49,812
lt's so soft!

426
00:35:53,017 --> 00:35:54,517
Iinuma! I want the truth!

427
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:56,653
That man's here!

428
00:35:57,288 --> 00:35:58,788
My husband...

429
00:36:03,027 --> 00:36:06,085
My ex-husband...I'd know
that drunken voice anywhere

430
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:11,501
I'm going!

431
00:36:11,969 --> 00:36:13,469
Your master's leaving

432
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:14,989
Hands off!

433
00:36:15,039 --> 00:36:16,190
I'm not drunk!

434
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:17,740
My sandals!

435
00:36:19,777 --> 00:36:21,365
Iinuma! Where's Tomoe gone?

436
00:36:22,780 --> 00:36:24,603
I told you, she's at her aunt's

437
00:36:25,316 --> 00:36:26,816
You're lying!

438
00:36:27,151 --> 00:36:30,680
PIease! Keep your voice down!
There are elderly people here!

439
00:36:31,389 --> 00:36:32,874
To hell with her

440
00:36:32,924 --> 00:36:34,424
Listen, Iinuma...

441
00:36:35,259 --> 00:36:38,494
lf I'm not good enough for Tomoe
she's welcome to leave

442
00:36:40,064 --> 00:36:41,564
But Iinuma...

443
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:44,291
...I've got a bone to pick
with you

444
00:36:45,503 --> 00:36:48,444
You went to His Lordship
and got him to divorce us

445
00:36:49,807 --> 00:36:52,689
Squire Koda, I've told you
time and time again...

446
00:36:54,478 --> 00:36:55,978
Shut up!

447
00:36:56,480 --> 00:36:59,303
You made me a joke
in front of the whole castle!

448
00:37:01,452 --> 00:37:02,952
I demand satisfaction!

449
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:05,640
Squire Koda!

450
00:37:05,690 --> 00:37:07,190
My sword!

451
00:37:08,125 --> 00:37:09,625
Stop this, will you?!

452
00:37:11,829 --> 00:37:13,329
Tomoe...

453
00:37:14,432 --> 00:37:17,137
Where've you been
till this hour of the night?

454
00:37:19,270 --> 00:37:21,622
Where I go is no one's business
but mine

455
00:37:22,974 --> 00:37:24,474
And I'll say this, too

456
00:37:26,377 --> 00:37:29,141
I am not your wife now
lt's 'Miss Tomoe' to you

457
00:37:36,754 --> 00:37:38,254
Tomoe! Get inside!

458
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,760
Perhaps that's enough?

459
00:37:45,496 --> 00:37:46,996
Who are you?!

460
00:37:53,838 --> 00:37:55,896
I am Seibei Iguchi
friend to Iinuma

461
00:37:59,377 --> 00:38:02,318
Perhaps I could accept
your challenge in his name?

462
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:05,369
But here we are in the town

463
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:09,452
And you are drunk

464
00:38:12,590 --> 00:38:16,119
Let's settle this another time
when the alcohol has worn off

465
00:38:23,901 --> 00:38:26,371
lf you've put yourself forward
this way...

466
00:38:29,006 --> 00:38:30,711
...you must know how to fight

467
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:32,975
I make no such claim

468
00:38:35,012 --> 00:38:36,512
Fine. We fight tomorrow

469
00:38:40,351 --> 00:38:41,851
Tomorrow?

470
00:38:42,186 --> 00:38:45,303
By the river behind Hannyaji
Temple, at the 8th hour?

471
00:38:51,228 --> 00:38:52,728
Done

472
00:38:53,297 --> 00:38:54,797
Behind Hannyaji, 8th hour

473
00:38:59,103 --> 00:39:00,603
See you

474
00:39:13,117 --> 00:39:14,617
Seibei, he's serious!

475
00:39:17,488 --> 00:39:18,988
Are you?

476
00:39:19,557 --> 00:39:21,057
I had no choice

477
00:39:21,726 --> 00:39:23,226
He's good with a sword

478
00:39:24,829 --> 00:39:26,329
lt'll work out

479
00:39:27,431 --> 00:39:28,931
I'll say good night

480
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:31,288
Don't tell Tomoe about this

481
00:39:37,808 --> 00:39:39,308
Wait!

482
00:39:43,414 --> 00:39:46,119
What if you kill him?
The CIan forbids dueling

483
00:39:47,485 --> 00:39:48,985
I'll think of something

484
00:39:51,188 --> 00:39:52,688
Good night

485
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:11,407
Naota...

486
00:40:50,014 --> 00:40:51,514
We're going

487
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:56,118
Ito!

488
00:41:05,629 --> 00:41:09,217
Yu Tzu said: Harmony is the
greatest beneficence of the rites

489
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:12,635
Good morning

490
00:41:22,947 --> 00:41:24,447
Sit down!

491
00:41:36,026 --> 00:41:37,526
I'm leaving

492
00:42:29,747 --> 00:42:31,247
This is no good. I'm slow

493
00:43:05,783 --> 00:43:07,312
You think you can take me?

494
00:43:08,452 --> 00:43:09,937
Damn right!

495
00:43:09,987 --> 00:43:11,487
Then get ready

496
00:43:16,627 --> 00:43:18,127
He's afraid!

497
00:43:23,167 --> 00:43:24,667
Hold it!

498
00:43:26,870 --> 00:43:29,105
I said last night
I'd take your place!

499
00:43:31,008 --> 00:43:31,959
I should do this

500
00:43:32,009 --> 00:43:34,773
You're no match for him
Go over there and watch

501
00:43:37,815 --> 00:43:41,050
I'm sorry I'm late, Squire Koda
I will be your opponent

502
00:43:43,487 --> 00:43:44,987
What's that stick?

503
00:43:46,223 --> 00:43:49,105
My school of swordfighting
uses this for practice

504
00:43:50,894 --> 00:43:52,776
Do you mock me?
Draw your sword!

505
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:57,534
A sword might kill
This stick will not

506
00:43:59,970 --> 00:44:01,617
lt will break bones at worst

507
00:44:04,408 --> 00:44:08,231
I won't take this from a samurai
of your rank! I'll cut you down!

508
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:38,712
Watch for the draw-and-slash!

509
00:44:44,548 --> 00:44:46,048
You can still apologize

510
00:44:48,719 --> 00:44:50,366
The apology is yours to make

511
00:45:37,134 --> 00:45:39,016
With a real sword, you'd be dead

512
00:45:54,551 --> 00:45:56,051
Do you apologize?

513
00:45:57,888 --> 00:45:59,388
Or do you continue?

514
00:46:25,349 --> 00:46:27,996
Splash some water on him
That'll bring him to

515
00:46:29,219 --> 00:46:30,719
Come on, Iinuma

516
00:46:37,194 --> 00:46:38,694
You're all right?

517
00:46:40,697 --> 00:46:42,579
Don't tell Miss Tomoe
about this

518
00:46:44,301 --> 00:46:45,801
Or anyone else, either

519
00:46:47,738 --> 00:46:49,238
Those men will talk

520
00:46:51,408 --> 00:46:53,172
No. A whipped dog
doesn't bark

521
00:47:19,837 --> 00:47:21,484
ls that soy sauce? Over here

522
00:47:54,738 --> 00:47:58,620
Excuse me for interrupting. I am
Zenemon Yogo, Master of the Watch

523
00:48:00,143 --> 00:48:01,643
I know that

524
00:48:02,279 --> 00:48:05,749
Are you the 'Twilight Seibei'
who thrashed Toyotaro Koda...

525
00:48:07,684 --> 00:48:10,625
...and left him with
a great big lump on his head?

526
00:48:12,756 --> 00:48:14,403
I didn't really 'thrash' him

527
00:48:19,062 --> 00:48:22,414
He asked for a match, and my
sword caught him on the head

528
00:48:23,700 --> 00:48:25,817
Koda is a drinking companion
of mine

529
00:48:27,104 --> 00:48:28,604
The other day...

530
00:48:31,608 --> 00:48:35,313
...he came crying to me, asking
if I would take revenge for him

531
00:48:42,219 --> 00:48:43,866
That's the kind of man he is

532
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:49,020
But it seems you can fight
What school are you?

533
00:48:52,829 --> 00:48:55,299
Many years ago I trained
under Toda-Sensei

534
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:01,720
So you're a disciple
of Jinsai Toda?

535
00:49:04,041 --> 00:49:05,570
I merely attended his dojo

536
00:49:09,112 --> 00:49:11,229
Perhaps we could
try a match one day

537
00:49:13,116 --> 00:49:16,527
I'd be no match for you
I'm afraid. lf you'll excuse me...

538
00:49:33,770 --> 00:49:37,181
I wish I wasn't getting old
I can't read once the sun sets

539
00:49:38,141 --> 00:49:40,435
First your teeth go
then it's your eyes

540
00:49:44,581 --> 00:49:46,081
And how's number three?

541
00:49:47,417 --> 00:49:48,917
That went long ago!

542
00:49:53,390 --> 00:49:55,095
That's it for today, everyone

543
00:50:12,642 --> 00:50:14,142
I'll be going

544
00:50:18,048 --> 00:50:19,548
Excuse me

545
00:50:24,755 --> 00:50:26,255
Sir Twilight's gone?

546
00:50:27,991 --> 00:50:29,491
Didn't you hear?

547
00:50:32,329 --> 00:50:35,799
The other day 'Sir Twilight' fought
the son of Captain Koda

548
00:50:37,801 --> 00:50:39,389
A fight? And what happened?

549
00:50:41,104 --> 00:50:42,604
Wood against steel

550
00:50:44,474 --> 00:50:47,121
Sir Twilight went bang!
Knocked him senseless

551
00:50:47,511 --> 00:50:48,962
He did?

552
00:50:49,012 --> 00:50:50,835
I always thought he was strange

553
00:50:51,915 --> 00:50:54,267
I never thought
he was a fighter, though

554
00:50:56,053 --> 00:50:58,876
Maybe we shouldn't
be calling him 'Sir Twilight'

555
00:51:00,290 --> 00:51:01,790
You think he knows?

556
00:51:02,259 --> 00:51:03,759
Sure he does

557
00:51:19,743 --> 00:51:21,243
Fumi! lt's raining!

558
00:51:30,620 --> 00:51:32,502
lt's raining!
ls the laundry in?

559
00:51:33,557 --> 00:51:35,057
Yes!

560
00:51:43,934 --> 00:51:45,434
Welcome home

561
00:51:46,269 --> 00:51:48,857
Miss Tomoe was here
She left you this letter

562
00:51:53,410 --> 00:51:56,351
She's got even nicer writing
than the schoolmaster

563
00:52:00,517 --> 00:52:01,635
Let me!

564
00:52:01,685 --> 00:52:03,185
No!

565
00:52:04,921 --> 00:52:08,332
I have finally learned what happened
from my elder brother

566
00:52:11,428 --> 00:52:13,722
I must apologize
for all the trouble...

567
00:52:16,933 --> 00:52:18,433
...I have caused you

568
00:52:19,703 --> 00:52:21,203
I am, however, delighted

569
00:52:26,610 --> 00:52:29,610
I very much want to see you
and thank you in person

570
00:52:32,215 --> 00:52:35,273
Today I intruded upon you and
with your daughters...

571
00:52:39,122 --> 00:52:41,592
...cleaned your house
and did your laundry

572
00:52:41,892 --> 00:52:45,009
PIease do not scold your daughters
for allowing me in

573
00:52:46,029 --> 00:52:49,029
I would like in the future
to be of what use I can.

574
00:52:54,538 --> 00:52:55,789
Written in haste

575
00:52:55,839 --> 00:52:57,897
To: Seibei Iguchi, Esq.
From: Tomoe

576
00:53:09,586 --> 00:53:12,115
Tomoe started coming
every second day or so

577
00:53:15,492 --> 00:53:18,727
The two of us looked forward
to coming home from school

578
00:53:20,797 --> 00:53:21,982
We're back!

579
00:53:22,032 --> 00:53:23,532
Hello!

580
00:53:26,503 --> 00:53:29,797
You know what the teacher
did today? He farted out loud!

581
00:53:38,949 --> 00:53:41,419
She cleaned with us
did laundry with us...

582
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:45,620
...and taught us to cook

583
00:53:51,494 --> 00:53:54,435
On rainy days we'd practice
calligraphy and sewing

584
00:53:56,166 --> 00:53:59,695
And she'd tell us all kinds
of stories, the like of which...

585
00:53:59,903 --> 00:54:01,432
...we'd never heard before

586
00:54:03,907 --> 00:54:05,407
Finished

587
00:54:08,612 --> 00:54:10,112
Bring this line over

588
00:54:11,982 --> 00:54:13,482
Finished!

589
00:54:13,683 --> 00:54:15,183
That's good, Ito!

590
00:54:16,820 --> 00:54:18,320
Hey! Stop it!

591
00:54:20,323 --> 00:54:22,675
Ito! Write on
your own paper, all right?

592
00:54:24,461 --> 00:54:25,961
No!

593
00:54:37,007 --> 00:54:38,507
Don't you look nice!

594
00:54:42,312 --> 00:54:45,664
How much fun it was to go off
to a festival in kimonos...

595
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:48,116
...she had made us

596
00:55:06,670 --> 00:55:08,170
Shoo! Go away!

597
00:56:04,561 --> 00:56:08,266
Samurai then were strictly
forbidden to attend the festivals...

598
00:56:09,366 --> 00:56:11,424
...of the peasants
and townsfolk...

599
00:56:14,270 --> 00:56:15,975
...but Tomoe cared not a whit

600
00:56:18,775 --> 00:56:20,539
I remember well what
she said:

601
00:56:21,344 --> 00:56:24,579
lt was because of the peasants
that we lived as samurai

602
00:57:01,184 --> 00:57:04,536
Why are you catching them all?
We're using the same bait!

603
00:57:05,522 --> 00:57:07,874
You're trying too hard
The fish sense it

604
00:57:11,961 --> 00:57:15,019
Your shoulders are too stiff
lt's like swordfighting

605
00:57:16,666 --> 00:57:18,166
Aw, stop lecturing!

606
00:57:19,602 --> 00:57:21,102
Show me your rod

607
00:57:26,042 --> 00:57:27,542
This hook's too big!

608
00:57:34,584 --> 00:57:36,084
Seibei...

609
00:57:37,053 --> 00:57:38,553
...I want to talk to you

610
00:57:40,523 --> 00:57:42,023
lt's about Tomoe

611
00:57:44,861 --> 00:57:46,361
She's had a few proposals

612
00:57:49,699 --> 00:57:53,581
She's beautiful and talented
There's not many like her in our clan

613
00:57:57,607 --> 00:57:59,107
Any good ones?

614
00:58:00,143 --> 00:58:02,613
She won't say yes
and I can't pressure her

615
00:58:04,280 --> 00:58:07,338
I asked her, half in jest
if she'd like to marry you

616
00:58:09,452 --> 00:58:10,952
You what?!

617
00:58:11,754 --> 00:58:14,283
We may be old friends
but that isn't funny!

618
00:58:16,793 --> 00:58:18,440
She didn't take it as a joke

619
00:58:20,830 --> 00:58:22,535
She said she wouldn't mind...

620
00:58:25,134 --> 00:58:26,634
...and turned all red

621
00:58:32,308 --> 00:58:34,896
That's enough!
You're both making fun of me!

622
00:58:40,049 --> 00:58:41,549
You dolt!

623
00:58:43,186 --> 00:58:44,686
She was serious

624
00:58:45,321 --> 00:58:46,821
Stop it

625
00:58:50,894 --> 00:58:52,394
Listen...

626
00:58:53,696 --> 00:58:57,048
...I've already put her through hell
marrying her to Koda

627
00:59:02,772 --> 00:59:06,183
lf it's all right with you
I'd like to make that up to her

628
00:59:10,079 --> 00:59:11,579
lt's a bit sudden...

629
00:59:20,757 --> 00:59:24,404
I don't need an answer now
but I will within two or three days

630
00:59:28,031 --> 00:59:29,531
I might have to go to Edo

631
00:59:31,901 --> 00:59:34,665
You've been really busy lately
What's going on?

632
00:59:35,371 --> 00:59:36,900
You probably haven't heard

633
00:59:39,409 --> 00:59:40,909
His Lordship's dead

634
00:59:42,879 --> 00:59:44,379
A month ago

635
00:59:49,085 --> 00:59:50,585
He is?

636
00:59:51,721 --> 00:59:53,603
Why have they kept that
from us?

637
00:59:55,491 --> 00:59:58,314
They're not agreed on
who's going to succeed him

638
01:00:01,898 --> 01:00:04,956
The Castle Warden, Lord Hori
has asked the Shogun...

639
01:00:07,637 --> 01:00:11,401
...for permission to adopt
His Lordship's third boy, Tadaatsu...

640
01:00:13,676 --> 01:00:15,323
...and seize control himself

641
01:00:17,246 --> 01:00:20,867
lf that happens the clan will split
and blood will wash away blood

642
01:00:20,917 --> 01:00:23,622
I might not come through this
unscathed myself

643
01:00:26,990 --> 01:00:30,284
So if you could give me an answer
before I leave for Edo

644
01:00:36,199 --> 01:00:37,699
All right

645
01:00:39,769 --> 01:00:41,269
I'll answer you

646
01:00:44,674 --> 01:00:48,497
I'm very grateful to Tomoe for
all she's done for my daughters...

647
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:54,530
...all the cooking and sewing
and everything else

648
01:00:56,919 --> 01:00:58,507
lt's like a dream come true

649
01:01:05,361 --> 01:01:06,861
However...

650
01:01:08,564 --> 01:01:12,387
...having her come to my house
as my wife is something else again

651
01:01:18,741 --> 01:01:21,623
She's a daughter of the Iinumas
a 400-koku family

652
01:01:24,714 --> 01:01:28,361
She doesn't know what life is like
for a 50-koku petty samurai

653
01:01:31,020 --> 01:01:33,667
Are you sure you're not
under-estimating her?

654
01:01:35,825 --> 01:01:37,530
She's very much her own woman

655
01:01:39,328 --> 01:01:40,828
lt'd be fine at the start

656
01:01:43,433 --> 01:01:47,021
But when it sunk in that 50-koku
would be her life forever...

657
01:01:48,871 --> 01:01:50,371
...she'd be sorry

658
01:01:54,777 --> 01:01:56,277
My late wife was

659
01:02:00,249 --> 01:02:01,778
Hers was a 150-koku family

660
01:02:04,187 --> 01:02:06,539
She never got used to
the fall in status

661
01:02:09,325 --> 01:02:12,512
Rise in the world, she told me
or my family will grieve

662
01:02:12,562 --> 01:02:15,209
She said that all the time
after she got sick

663
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:20,705
I don't want to put Tomoe
through that torment

664
01:02:34,217 --> 01:02:35,717
Tomoe's not 15 or 16

665
01:02:38,488 --> 01:02:40,958
I'm sure she'd thought about
what she said

666
01:02:43,826 --> 01:02:45,326
No more

667
01:02:47,330 --> 01:02:48,830
Let's forget this

668
01:02:54,036 --> 01:02:55,536
Let's try up there

669
01:02:58,808 --> 01:03:00,308
lt's a girl!

670
01:03:08,384 --> 01:03:09,884
What a stink!

671
01:03:17,593 --> 01:03:19,093
Rise to Lord Buddha

672
01:03:21,564 --> 01:03:23,064
Eat your fill in heaven!

673
01:03:26,035 --> 01:03:27,535
Let's call it a day

674
01:03:36,012 --> 01:03:37,964
From that day forward
Miss Tomoe stopped coming...

675
01:03:38,014 --> 01:03:39,514
...to our house

676
01:03:45,054 --> 01:03:46,554
Make way!

677
01:03:47,824 --> 01:03:49,324
Stand aside!

678
01:03:49,559 --> 01:03:51,059
Turning left!

679
01:04:01,370 --> 01:04:02,870
The Warden has returned!

680
01:04:24,760 --> 01:04:26,260
Go!

681
01:04:36,038 --> 01:04:37,538
What's that?!

682
01:04:38,140 --> 01:04:39,640
lt's the alarm!

683
01:04:48,484 --> 01:04:50,425
Stop what you're doing and listen

684
01:04:51,988 --> 01:04:55,164
I have important news
from Lord Hori, Castle Warden...

685
01:04:56,425 --> 01:04:58,601
...who returned
this morning from Edo

686
01:04:59,729 --> 01:05:03,670
The 12th head of the Unasaka CIan
Lord Tadatomo, died of measles...

687
01:05:06,302 --> 01:05:08,243
...at the beginning of this month

688
01:05:08,671 --> 01:05:10,171
He was 32 years old

689
01:05:14,210 --> 01:05:17,504
He was a good and wise ruler
intelligent and tolerant...

690
01:05:19,949 --> 01:05:21,449
...a true hero

691
01:05:23,486 --> 01:05:26,486
Only last spring we had
the honor of meeting him...

692
01:05:27,556 --> 01:05:29,261
...and having him speak to us

693
01:05:32,495 --> 01:05:35,083
Iguchi, you haven't
forgotten that, I'm sure

694
01:05:39,335 --> 01:05:41,335
What a fine and gentle man
he was!

695
01:05:46,175 --> 01:05:48,645
Senior retainers will
remain in the castle

696
01:05:49,912 --> 01:05:54,323
The rest of you are to leave and pray
for the repose of His Lordship's soul

697
01:06:08,798 --> 01:06:10,298
This could mean open war!

698
01:06:11,667 --> 01:06:13,167
I doubt that...

699
01:06:17,873 --> 01:06:21,160
...but Lord Hori's sure to go after
His Lordships reformers

700
01:06:21,210 --> 01:06:22,710
Dispositions'?

701
01:06:22,945 --> 01:06:24,445
Yes

702
01:06:24,680 --> 01:06:26,680
Which side is
our Commissioner on?

703
01:06:27,750 --> 01:06:29,750
The reformers
or the Hori faction?

704
01:06:31,020 --> 01:06:32,667
He'll be with the mainstream

705
01:06:35,825 --> 01:06:37,325
Just like me

706
01:06:42,898 --> 01:06:47,192
While there were fearsome rumors
that the Castle was preparing for war...

707
01:06:49,238 --> 01:06:52,590
...it didn't seem to involve
petty samurai like my father

708
01:07:29,645 --> 01:07:31,145
All right?

709
01:07:32,848 --> 01:07:36,142
We wanted to ask Father
why Miss Tomoe no longer came...

710
01:07:41,791 --> 01:07:43,791
...but for some reason
we couldn't

711
01:07:46,262 --> 01:07:49,144
This was because even in
our children's hearts...

712
01:07:51,200 --> 01:07:53,905
...we knew something
had happened between them

713
01:07:59,208 --> 01:08:00,708
Squire Iguchi!

714
01:08:05,014 --> 01:08:08,778
I'm sorry you've come for nothing
My husband isn't back from Edo

715
01:08:10,686 --> 01:08:12,333
I expect him in a day or two

716
01:08:16,459 --> 01:08:19,635
Has he written anything about
what's happening in Edo?

717
01:08:21,363 --> 01:08:22,863
No

718
01:08:22,932 --> 01:08:24,755
There was a letter yesterday...

719
01:08:27,837 --> 01:08:31,895
...but all he talked about was what
he wants to eat when he gets home

720
01:08:32,808 --> 01:08:34,308
That's good

721
01:08:35,578 --> 01:08:38,578
I'm sure you know
they're handing down dispositions

722
01:08:41,450 --> 01:08:44,508
Some people have even been
ordered to commit suicide

723
01:08:45,688 --> 01:08:48,864
I was worried about what
might have happened to Iinuma

724
01:08:51,460 --> 01:08:53,342
I'm happy to hear he's all right

725
01:08:56,198 --> 01:08:58,374
Give him my regards
when he gets home

726
01:09:00,236 --> 01:09:01,736
You came just for that?

727
01:09:03,672 --> 01:09:05,091
Yes

728
01:09:05,141 --> 01:09:06,641
Good day

729
01:09:11,514 --> 01:09:13,014
lt was very kind of you

730
01:09:23,659 --> 01:09:25,159
Carry on

731
01:09:27,329 --> 01:09:28,829
Where's Squire Iguchi?

732
01:09:29,165 --> 01:09:30,665
He went away

733
01:09:33,669 --> 01:09:35,169
Where are you going?

734
01:09:35,804 --> 01:09:37,862
Squire Iguchi may still be
close by

735
01:09:39,308 --> 01:09:40,896
Why do you want to see him?

736
01:09:42,411 --> 01:09:43,911
No reason in particular

737
01:09:46,448 --> 01:09:49,506
I haven't seen him for a while
I'd like to say hello

738
01:09:50,019 --> 01:09:51,519
Wait!

739
01:09:57,993 --> 01:09:59,493
Tomoe...

740
01:10:00,095 --> 01:10:03,447
...it is unseemly for
a young woman to be seen talking...

741
01:10:03,566 --> 01:10:05,566
...with some samurai on the street

742
01:10:07,336 --> 01:10:10,865
And you are a returned bride
with a proposal being discussed

743
01:10:11,040 --> 01:10:14,804
You shouldn't be doing that
in broad daylight with people around

744
01:10:19,715 --> 01:10:22,891
I've been meaning to tell you that
for a long time now

745
01:10:25,754 --> 01:10:28,459
What's wrong with a girl
talking to a samurai?

746
01:10:32,494 --> 01:10:35,199
Are you questioning
your elder brother's wife?

747
01:10:35,798 --> 01:10:37,298
Shouldn't I?

748
01:10:37,866 --> 01:10:39,366
You should not

749
01:10:40,269 --> 01:10:42,739
A young women
does not question her elders

750
01:11:05,828 --> 01:11:08,475
With 60 from last month
that comes to 550 mon

751
01:11:11,934 --> 01:11:13,434
Could I have a receipt?

752
01:11:18,841 --> 01:11:21,958
You know the bath fee went up
to seven mon last month

753
01:11:24,680 --> 01:11:26,444
Prices are going up everywhere

754
01:11:29,518 --> 01:11:31,576
Could you pay more
for these cages?

755
01:11:33,289 --> 01:11:35,074
With things as unsettled
as they are...

756
01:11:35,124 --> 01:11:36,947
...no one's buying insect cages

757
01:11:39,628 --> 01:11:41,451
Could you ask your boss
for me?

758
01:11:44,500 --> 01:11:46,000
Well, I'll ask

759
01:11:47,636 --> 01:11:50,106
I take this work
as seriously as my duties

760
01:11:50,372 --> 01:11:51,872
I understand that

761
01:11:52,474 --> 01:11:53,974
lf you'll excuse me

762
01:11:57,980 --> 01:11:59,480
Come on

763
01:12:19,401 --> 01:12:20,901
We're not thieves

764
01:12:22,037 --> 01:12:25,507
We're just picking up some
insect cages from Squire Iguchi.

765
01:12:28,444 --> 01:12:29,944
ls he doing piece-work?

766
01:12:45,260 --> 01:12:46,760
Hello!

767
01:12:47,262 --> 01:12:48,547
Hello!

768
01:12:48,597 --> 01:12:50,097
Who is it?

769
01:12:52,701 --> 01:12:54,201
Commissioner Kusaka

770
01:13:02,478 --> 01:13:03,978
lt's very late, I know

771
01:13:05,214 --> 01:13:08,272
I'd like you to accompany me
to Lord Hori's quarters

772
01:13:09,852 --> 01:13:11,352
Yes, sir

773
01:13:14,656 --> 01:13:17,126
They said you don't need
full formal dress

774
01:13:18,594 --> 01:13:20,094
Just a hakama skirt

775
01:13:36,779 --> 01:13:39,190
So you're Iguchi's girl?
How old are you?

776
01:13:41,817 --> 01:13:43,317
Five

777
01:13:44,987 --> 01:13:46,487
You're a sweetheart

778
01:13:52,027 --> 01:13:53,527
I'm ready

779
01:14:03,172 --> 01:14:04,760
Kayano...you all get to bed

780
01:14:11,647 --> 01:14:13,147
Let's sleep

781
01:14:33,335 --> 01:14:35,511
Seibei Iguchi
of the Castle Stores...

782
01:14:35,938 --> 01:14:37,438
That'll do

783
01:14:38,373 --> 01:14:39,873
Iguchi, come over here

784
01:14:53,388 --> 01:14:57,388
We called you here this late because
an awkward situation has arisen

785
01:14:59,828 --> 01:15:03,063
You know there was a revolt
among our retainers in Edo?

786
01:15:04,833 --> 01:15:06,333
Yes, sir

787
01:15:07,503 --> 01:15:10,208
Fortunately no word of this
reached the Shogun

788
01:15:11,607 --> 01:15:15,665
His Lordship ordered Shima Hasegawa
and his faction to commit suicide

789
01:15:16,411 --> 01:15:20,352
But one of Lord Hasegawa's men
Zenemon Yogo, Master of the Watch...

790
01:15:21,583 --> 01:15:25,171
...says he was merely following
the orders of his superior...

791
01:15:29,224 --> 01:15:32,277
...asks why he should be punished
and refuses to commit suicide

792
01:15:32,327 --> 01:15:35,091
lf you want me dead
come and kill me,' he says!

793
01:15:40,869 --> 01:15:44,869
And with these disgraceful words
has barricaded himself in his house

794
01:15:47,910 --> 01:15:51,851
This evening we sent our Master
of Foot, Genba Hattori, against him

795
01:15:53,949 --> 01:15:56,654
Zenemon Yogo! I come
at the order of the clan!

796
01:16:02,157 --> 01:16:03,657
But he died himself

797
01:16:15,537 --> 01:16:17,066
He's a 'one-sword' fighter

798
01:16:19,541 --> 01:16:21,364
No one in the clan
is his match

799
01:16:23,645 --> 01:16:26,468
We were talking about who
to send against him...

800
01:16:27,282 --> 01:16:28,782
...and your name came up

801
01:16:32,421 --> 01:16:33,921
Iguchi, raise your head

802
01:16:39,394 --> 01:16:42,335
You're a 'short-sword' fighter
of the Toda school?

803
01:16:44,333 --> 01:16:46,818
lt's been years
since Toda-Sensei taught me

804
01:16:46,868 --> 01:16:48,397
I merely attended his dojo

805
01:16:52,708 --> 01:16:54,472
We don't have time
for modesty

806
01:16:56,645 --> 01:16:59,762
We've learned that you were
an instructor at his dojo

807
01:17:02,317 --> 01:17:06,199
He must be beaten inside his house
The short sword will help there

808
01:17:06,455 --> 01:17:08,866
That is another reason
we have chosen you

809
01:17:13,962 --> 01:17:16,197
Kill Zenemon Yogo
by twilight tomorrow

810
01:17:20,469 --> 01:17:23,292
That is an order from
the clan's Senior Retainer

811
01:17:29,811 --> 01:17:31,869
Kusaka...what's this man's stipend?

812
01:17:33,849 --> 01:17:35,349
50 koku

813
01:17:35,684 --> 01:17:37,566
20 koku bespoken
for a net of 30

814
01:17:39,821 --> 01:17:43,468
That must be hard, with two young
daughters and an aged mother

815
01:17:45,527 --> 01:17:47,644
Bring us the head
of Zenemon Yogo...

816
01:17:49,598 --> 01:17:51,127
...and life will be easier

817
01:17:52,134 --> 01:17:53,634
Do you accept?

818
01:17:58,373 --> 01:17:59,873
Answer him

819
01:18:01,410 --> 01:18:02,910
This is an honor

820
01:18:05,847 --> 01:18:07,347
You shut up!

821
01:18:08,116 --> 01:18:09,616
Well?

822
01:18:13,722 --> 01:18:15,222
By your leave...

823
01:18:22,030 --> 01:18:25,265
I am ashamed to say that
over many years of hardship...

824
01:18:28,637 --> 01:18:31,931
...with two daughters, a sick wife
and an aged mother...

825
01:18:34,176 --> 01:18:36,646
...I have lost the desire
to wield a sword

826
01:18:43,418 --> 01:18:45,712
A serious fight
the killing of a man...

827
01:18:50,325 --> 01:18:54,148
...requires animal ferocity and
calm disregard for one's own life

828
01:18:57,632 --> 01:18:59,808
I have neither of those
within me now

829
01:19:03,605 --> 01:19:05,105
Perhaps in a month...

830
01:19:10,479 --> 01:19:13,632
...alone with the beasts in the hills
I could get them back

831
01:19:13,682 --> 01:19:16,623
But tomorrow, I am afraid
is completely impossible

832
01:19:23,492 --> 01:19:26,609
I ask that you extend
the honor of this commission...

833
01:19:29,798 --> 01:19:31,298
...to another man

834
01:19:35,437 --> 01:19:37,378
What complete
and utter nonsense!

835
01:19:40,142 --> 01:19:43,259
We are not here for foolishness
from a petty samurai!

836
01:19:46,314 --> 01:19:48,255
Your clan orders you
to kill Yogo

837
01:19:50,719 --> 01:19:52,219
Do you understand that?!

838
01:19:53,488 --> 01:19:56,017
The CIan's orders are
His Lordship's orders

839
01:19:57,425 --> 01:19:59,895
The very thought of refusal
is an offense!

840
01:20:01,096 --> 01:20:04,743
You are relieved of your post!
You are expelled from the clan!

841
01:20:06,134 --> 01:20:07,634
PIease, Warden...

842
01:20:09,337 --> 01:20:11,631
What do you say, Iguchi?
Do you accept?

843
01:20:14,776 --> 01:20:16,228
Of course he does!

844
01:20:16,278 --> 01:20:17,778
Don't you!

845
01:20:19,714 --> 01:20:21,714
May I request
an evening or two...

846
01:20:24,753 --> 01:20:26,517
...in which to give my answer?

847
01:20:28,190 --> 01:20:29,690
You may not!!

848
01:20:30,625 --> 01:20:32,125
You will answer now!

849
01:21:03,291 --> 01:21:04,791
I obey

850
01:21:08,296 --> 01:21:09,825
I accept the commission...

851
01:21:13,468 --> 01:21:14,968
...to kill Zenemon Yogo

852
01:21:18,406 --> 01:21:19,906
Well said!

853
01:21:20,642 --> 01:21:23,289
An officer will call
at the hour of the snake

854
01:21:24,379 --> 01:21:25,967
Have your preparations made

855
01:21:28,750 --> 01:21:30,250
Withdraw

856
01:21:54,676 --> 01:21:56,176
Iguchi...

857
01:22:00,482 --> 01:22:02,776
Don't worry. Who's Zenemon
Yogo anyway?

858
01:22:02,951 --> 01:22:04,451
You're sure to win

859
01:22:06,054 --> 01:22:07,642
I have decided exactly that

860
01:22:09,824 --> 01:22:10,976
Good

861
01:22:11,026 --> 01:22:13,849
One should, however
always prepare for the worst

862
01:22:16,698 --> 01:22:19,050
That's true. The worst
can always happen

863
01:22:21,169 --> 01:22:24,051
ln that event, Commissioner
this will be farewell

864
01:22:29,978 --> 01:22:32,507
Thank you for everything
you've done for me

865
01:22:35,583 --> 01:22:38,583
PIease convey my regards
to my colleagues in Stores

866
01:22:42,157 --> 01:22:43,657
I understand. And, uh...

867
01:22:44,092 --> 01:22:47,268
...I'll take responsibility for
those you leave behind

868
01:22:50,632 --> 01:22:52,396
I'll see they are looked after

869
01:22:57,739 --> 01:22:59,239
That's a relief to hear

870
01:23:03,111 --> 01:23:04,611
All the best to you

871
01:24:59,594 --> 01:25:01,711
A strange noise made me
open my eyes

872
01:25:05,800 --> 01:25:09,270
Looking for the sound, I saw
my father sharpening his sword

873
01:25:12,740 --> 01:25:16,269
He looked so strange it was hard
to believe he was my father

874
01:25:21,549 --> 01:25:24,431
I still remember clearly
how he looked that night

875
01:27:04,385 --> 01:27:05,885
The Heart Sutra:

876
01:27:11,359 --> 01:27:15,064
The bodhisative clearly saw
the emptiness of the five states...

877
01:27:16,064 --> 01:27:18,240
...thus relieving misfortune and pain

878
01:27:23,738 --> 01:27:26,385
Form is only emptiness
emptiness only form---

879
01:27:32,847 --> 01:27:34,347
We're going

880
01:27:35,683 --> 01:27:37,183
Kayano!

881
01:27:41,456 --> 01:27:45,044
The Master said: a man cunning
of word and smiling of face...

882
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:49,160
...is rarely benevolent
Tseng Tzu said: Each day---

883
01:28:02,944 --> 01:28:04,473
Naota, do something for me

884
01:28:05,747 --> 01:28:07,131
Yup

885
01:28:07,181 --> 01:28:10,298
You know Miss Tomoe's house
in Nishikicho, don't you?

886
01:28:12,987 --> 01:28:14,472
Yup

887
01:28:14,522 --> 01:28:16,463
Go there, and speak to
Miss Tomoe

888
01:28:18,993 --> 01:28:20,493
Now, this is important

889
01:28:22,030 --> 01:28:24,030
You have to see
Miss Tomoe herself

890
01:28:25,700 --> 01:28:27,200
And then say...

891
01:28:28,603 --> 01:28:31,955
...'I'm really very sorry, but
could you come right away?

892
01:28:33,808 --> 01:28:35,925
I'll explain why
when you get here.'

893
01:28:38,513 --> 01:28:40,013
All right?

894
01:28:41,449 --> 01:28:42,949
I'm really very sorry...

895
01:28:46,087 --> 01:28:48,028
...but could you come
right away?

896
01:28:50,224 --> 01:28:51,509
I'll explain why...

897
01:28:51,559 --> 01:28:53,059
Uh, I'll explain why...

898
01:28:53,628 --> 01:28:55,628
I'll explain why
when you get here

899
01:28:58,132 --> 01:28:59,632
When you get here

900
01:29:01,469 --> 01:29:02,969
That's fine. Hurry

901
01:29:15,883 --> 01:29:17,530
Look where she laid her egg!

902
01:29:23,124 --> 01:29:24,624
Could you come...

903
01:29:27,862 --> 01:29:29,862
I'll explain why
when you get here

904
01:29:35,002 --> 01:29:37,060
Whatever's the matter
at this hour?

905
01:29:39,640 --> 01:29:41,140
I'm really very sorry...

906
01:29:43,978 --> 01:29:45,919
...but could you come
right away?

907
01:29:47,982 --> 01:29:49,482
When you get here...uh...

908
01:29:53,488 --> 01:29:54,988
He'll explain why?

909
01:29:55,957 --> 01:29:58,251
Squire Seibei sent you
to tell me that?

910
01:30:00,027 --> 01:30:01,527
All right. I'll get ready

911
01:30:31,259 --> 01:30:32,759
I didn't think you'd come

912
01:30:52,747 --> 01:30:55,217
The clan has ordered me
to go and fight...

913
01:30:58,152 --> 01:30:59,652
...another retainer

914
01:31:03,458 --> 01:31:06,928
I'm going out under orders
so I must be properly dressed...

915
01:31:09,263 --> 01:31:11,086
...and I can't do my hair alone

916
01:31:13,167 --> 01:31:15,284
I'm in a bind
so I asked you to come

917
01:31:18,406 --> 01:31:20,994
lf you can spare the time
could you help me?

918
01:31:24,078 --> 01:31:25,578
When do you have to go?

919
01:31:27,181 --> 01:31:28,681
The hour of the snake

920
01:31:29,484 --> 01:31:30,984
There's not much time

921
01:31:33,454 --> 01:31:34,954
Where's your kimono?

922
01:31:35,089 --> 01:31:36,589
lt's laid out over there

923
01:31:41,229 --> 01:31:42,729
Naota, boil some water

924
01:32:23,738 --> 01:32:25,238
Who's coming for you?

925
01:32:26,407 --> 01:32:27,907
A clan officer

926
01:32:30,311 --> 01:32:32,487
Naota, will you wait
out by the gate?

927
01:32:37,318 --> 01:32:39,023
Sit down. I'll comb your hair

928
01:33:01,042 --> 01:33:02,542
May I ask why...

929
01:33:06,347 --> 01:33:08,052
...you're going out to fight?

930
01:33:14,322 --> 01:33:15,910
I can't refuse a clan order

931
01:33:19,493 --> 01:33:21,728
Petty I may be
but I'm still a samurai

932
01:33:47,355 --> 01:33:48,855
Bamboo baskets, hampers!

933
01:33:54,128 --> 01:33:55,628
Bamboo baskets, hampers!

934
01:35:08,669 --> 01:35:10,169
Your elder brother...

935
01:35:15,476 --> 01:35:17,770
...asked if I would
take you as my wife

936
01:35:20,514 --> 01:35:22,014
I refused

937
01:35:23,951 --> 01:35:25,451
Did you know that?

938
01:35:29,290 --> 01:35:30,790
Yes, I did

939
01:35:33,194 --> 01:35:34,694
But...

940
01:35:36,530 --> 01:35:38,030
But since that day...

941
01:35:40,034 --> 01:35:41,534
...when I told him no...

942
01:35:44,071 --> 01:35:46,071
...I've started thinking
about you

943
01:35:55,750 --> 01:35:58,397
Now I think of it
ever since we were small...

944
01:36:03,457 --> 01:36:05,457
...and I made dolls
to give you...

945
01:36:08,195 --> 01:36:11,430
...I always dreamed one day
you'd come to me as my wife

946
01:36:16,871 --> 01:36:19,988
That dream stayed with me
even after I got married...

947
01:36:24,678 --> 01:36:26,178
...and you married Koda

948
01:36:29,717 --> 01:36:31,217
lt's never faded

949
01:36:40,194 --> 01:36:42,488
I'm going out now
to fight to the death

950
01:36:46,634 --> 01:36:49,045
I'm going to win
and return to this house

951
01:36:52,072 --> 01:36:54,248
At that time, if I were
to ask you...

952
01:36:58,112 --> 01:36:59,612
...to be my wife...

953
01:37:03,184 --> 01:37:04,684
...would you accept?

954
01:37:12,993 --> 01:37:14,993
A few days ago I had
a proposal...

955
01:37:18,866 --> 01:37:20,395
...from a retainer in Aizu

956
01:37:21,635 --> 01:37:23,135
I accepted.

957
01:37:38,485 --> 01:37:39,985
I've been very rude

958
01:37:43,457 --> 01:37:45,927
I should never have asked you
to come here

959
01:37:50,564 --> 01:37:52,064
No

960
01:37:52,867 --> 01:37:54,455
I'm happy that you asked me

961
01:38:08,549 --> 01:38:10,049
I've been a fool

962
01:38:14,288 --> 01:38:16,288
PIease forget everything
I've said

963
01:38:23,898 --> 01:38:25,721
Really? A retainer from Aizu...

964
01:38:30,838 --> 01:38:32,338
That sounds like

965
01:38:45,419 --> 01:38:46,637
Are they here?

966
01:38:46,687 --> 01:38:48,187
Yup

967
01:38:49,924 --> 01:38:51,424
Well, I'll be going

968
01:38:56,664 --> 01:38:58,664
Thank you very much
for everything

969
01:39:03,137 --> 01:39:04,637
Um...

970
01:39:06,240 --> 01:39:09,240
...I'm afraid I can't wait here
until you come back

971
01:39:13,580 --> 01:39:15,168
I pray with all my heart...

972
01:39:22,456 --> 01:39:25,338
...that luck is with you
and you come back safely

973
01:39:47,014 --> 01:39:49,366
Naota, see Miss Tomoe home
when she goes

974
01:39:52,853 --> 01:39:54,353
Take care of the kids

975
01:40:56,517 --> 01:40:58,017
Mrs Iguchi...

976
01:40:59,686 --> 01:41:01,186
...how are you today?

977
01:41:03,624 --> 01:41:05,124
Fine, thank you

978
01:41:08,362 --> 01:41:11,009
Of which household
would you be the daughter?

979
01:41:15,235 --> 01:41:16,735
Me?

980
01:41:19,239 --> 01:41:20,739
I am ...

981
01:41:22,843 --> 01:41:25,078
...Squire Seibei's
childhood friend...

982
01:41:29,283 --> 01:41:30,783
...Tomoe

983
01:41:46,700 --> 01:41:48,200
Sir...

984
01:41:56,043 --> 01:41:57,543
Squire Iguchi?

985
01:42:01,748 --> 01:42:05,100
Zenemon Yogo has closed himself in
with the shutters down

986
01:42:10,457 --> 01:42:12,574
That is Genba Hattori
Master of Foot

987
01:42:14,895 --> 01:42:16,659
We should remove
his corpse...

988
01:42:17,865 --> 01:42:19,365
...but no one can get in

989
01:42:23,003 --> 01:42:24,503
Take care

990
01:42:26,573 --> 01:42:29,278
Zenemon Yogo is no longer human
He is a beast!

991
01:42:46,627 --> 01:42:48,127
Leave to enter!

992
01:43:23,230 --> 01:43:24,730
Sir Twilight...

993
01:43:39,513 --> 01:43:41,013
So they sent you?

994
01:43:46,453 --> 01:43:49,805
Zenemon Yogo...by order of
the clan, I come for your life

995
01:43:55,662 --> 01:43:57,162
Draw your sword, please

996
01:44:13,280 --> 01:44:14,780
Have a drink?

997
01:44:17,918 --> 01:44:20,682
I know you're all keyed up
but I'm going to run

998
01:44:22,923 --> 01:44:24,241
Run?

999
01:44:24,291 --> 01:44:25,791
Yep

1000
01:44:27,094 --> 01:44:29,446
I want you let me get away
lf you please

1001
01:44:39,473 --> 01:44:42,708
I didn't expect that from the clan's
best one-sword man

1002
01:44:46,046 --> 01:44:48,869
My orders are to kill you
I can't let you escape

1003
01:44:53,920 --> 01:44:56,625
Don't be so impatient
You can kill me any time

1004
01:44:59,526 --> 01:45:01,026
I'd like to talk to you

1005
01:45:03,430 --> 01:45:04,930
Have a seat

1006
01:45:11,838 --> 01:45:13,338
lt's a nice day

1007
01:45:16,376 --> 01:45:17,876
Sit down

1008
01:45:36,296 --> 01:45:37,796
What's going on?

1009
01:45:38,131 --> 01:45:39,631
They're talking

1010
01:45:47,607 --> 01:45:49,901
Even if you escaped
where would you go?

1011
01:45:53,146 --> 01:45:56,146
Over that mountain and I'm out
of the clan's domain

1012
01:45:58,985 --> 01:46:01,279
There are masterless samurai
everywhere

1013
01:46:02,189 --> 01:46:05,012
I can lose myself in them
go to Kyoto, to Edo...

1014
01:46:06,693 --> 01:46:08,516
lf I do that for a few years...

1015
01:46:09,029 --> 01:46:10,793
...the world will have changed

1016
01:46:13,367 --> 01:46:14,867
The samurai's day is done

1017
01:46:16,269 --> 01:46:18,210
This isn't the time
for that talk

1018
01:46:19,840 --> 01:46:21,369
Pick up your sword, please

1019
01:46:25,412 --> 01:46:27,588
I am under orders
from the clan to...

1020
01:46:28,849 --> 01:46:30,349
Like hell!

1021
01:46:34,087 --> 01:46:37,028
You're the clan's errand boy
out to claim a reward

1022
01:46:42,062 --> 01:46:44,238
Have a drink
I was an errand boy, too

1023
01:47:01,481 --> 01:47:03,128
I served Lord Shigemasa Toki

1024
01:47:05,986 --> 01:47:09,044
Twelve years ago he was ordered
to commit suicide...

1025
01:47:11,858 --> 01:47:14,269
...after a power struggle
within his clan

1026
01:47:16,163 --> 01:47:19,483
Then I wandered for seven years
with my wife and daughter...

1027
01:47:19,533 --> 01:47:21,356
...in search of a new situation

1028
01:47:26,239 --> 01:47:27,739
Seven?

1029
01:47:28,775 --> 01:47:30,275
With no income?

1030
01:47:32,345 --> 01:47:33,845
Of course not

1031
01:47:34,314 --> 01:47:37,784
I did manual labor and helped
peasants plant and harvest...

1032
01:47:40,821 --> 01:47:42,321
...to get a little rice

1033
01:47:43,557 --> 01:47:46,851
Or we'd slink into a temple
and beg alms there sometimes

1034
01:47:49,796 --> 01:47:53,560
Three years ago the Unasaka clan
made me an official retainer...

1035
01:47:55,535 --> 01:47:58,005
...but by then hardship
had killed my wife

1036
01:48:03,076 --> 01:48:06,311
I'm good with a sword
but I'm hard to get along with...

1037
01:48:09,583 --> 01:48:11,288
...and I can't hold my liquor

1038
01:48:16,423 --> 01:48:19,305
But this time I promised myself
it'd be different

1039
01:48:19,860 --> 01:48:22,507
I would do my duty
as a true Unasaka retainer

1040
01:48:23,029 --> 01:48:24,529
I worked hard to do that

1041
01:48:28,802 --> 01:48:30,860
My superior was
Lord Shima Hasegawa

1042
01:48:33,473 --> 01:48:35,825
He liked me, and did
all he could for me

1043
01:48:38,778 --> 01:48:40,278
To me...

1044
01:48:41,414 --> 01:48:44,414
...the tasks he assigned were
the tasks of the clan

1045
01:48:47,220 --> 01:48:51,161
His orders were the clan's orders
and I carried them out faithfully

1046
01:48:54,194 --> 01:48:56,194
What was wrong with that
Twilight?

1047
01:48:56,663 --> 01:48:58,839
Why do I have to
cut open my stomach?

1048
01:49:03,603 --> 01:49:05,485
I haven't come here
to answer...

1049
01:49:06,039 --> 01:49:07,539
...that kind of question

1050
01:49:15,916 --> 01:49:18,974
I heard your wife died
of consumption. ls that true?

1051
01:49:24,224 --> 01:49:25,812
I'm surprised you know that

1052
01:49:25,892 --> 01:49:28,186
And her fever went up
as night came on?

1053
01:49:30,964 --> 01:49:32,464
Yes

1054
01:49:33,934 --> 01:49:36,698
Consumption is a hard disease
And it's catching

1055
01:49:40,340 --> 01:49:43,516
My daughter died of consumption
caught from her mother

1056
01:49:46,513 --> 01:49:48,748
You're not the only one
who's suffered

1057
01:49:51,017 --> 01:49:52,546
How old was your daughter?

1058
01:49:54,854 --> 01:49:56,354
Sixteen

1059
01:50:02,429 --> 01:50:05,605
When she should have been
a bud swelling into bloom...

1060
01:50:07,334 --> 01:50:08,834
...she died...

1061
01:50:12,706 --> 01:50:15,411
...nothing but skin and bones
A sad, sad sight

1062
01:50:19,546 --> 01:50:21,134
I'm very sorry to hear that

1063
01:50:23,116 --> 01:50:24,616
Her ashes

1064
01:50:30,090 --> 01:50:32,207
She was a pretty girl
with pale skin

1065
01:50:45,005 --> 01:50:47,181
I guess Lord Hasegawa
took pity on me

1066
01:50:50,210 --> 01:50:53,268
He gave me money for a funeral
well above my station

1067
01:50:57,183 --> 01:50:58,683
lf only for that...

1068
01:50:59,919 --> 01:51:02,271
...I'm very much in
Lord Hasegawa's debt

1069
01:51:09,596 --> 01:51:11,096
What's your stipend?

1070
01:51:14,668 --> 01:51:16,168
50 koku

1071
01:51:18,672 --> 01:51:21,083
A sick wife, and children
all on 50 koku?

1072
01:51:24,911 --> 01:51:26,411
That must be hard

1073
01:51:32,419 --> 01:51:35,536
Doctor and medicine alone cost
a ryo and 2 bu a month

1074
01:51:42,429 --> 01:51:44,193
Piece work wouldn't cover that

1075
01:51:46,566 --> 01:51:49,624
I borrowed from relatives
but it still wasn't enough

1076
01:51:51,304 --> 01:51:54,245
Sometimes we didn't even have
tomorrow's rice left

1077
01:51:56,910 --> 01:52:00,439
I know how bad it feels to see
the bottom of your rice chest

1078
01:52:03,616 --> 01:52:05,145
You've had hard times, too

1079
01:52:07,020 --> 01:52:10,137
Where I really ran into trouble
was my wife's funeral

1080
01:52:13,126 --> 01:52:17,008
The family's main branch wanted
a funeral that wouldn't shame them

1081
01:52:18,665 --> 01:52:20,165
I couldn't afford it

1082
01:52:21,701 --> 01:52:24,171
I was desperate
so I finally sold my sword

1083
01:52:27,373 --> 01:52:30,373
lt was a fine sword
I'd inherited from my father...

1084
01:52:35,315 --> 01:52:38,020
...but I figured
the age of the sword was over

1085
01:52:45,892 --> 01:52:47,656
I'm afraid this is just bamboo

1086
01:52:57,403 --> 01:52:59,991
You're going to kill me
with a bamboo sword?

1087
01:53:04,544 --> 01:53:06,044
No

1088
01:53:07,180 --> 01:53:09,415
I learned short-sword
from Toda-Sensei

1089
01:53:11,885 --> 01:53:13,414
I meant to fight with that

1090
01:53:17,023 --> 01:53:18,523
Short-sword?

1091
01:53:20,126 --> 01:53:23,067
You mean to kill me
with some kind of cheap trick?

1092
01:53:25,431 --> 01:53:27,666
You're not taking me seriously
are you

1093
01:53:30,303 --> 01:53:31,803
Wait!

1094
01:53:31,938 --> 01:53:33,438
I won't have it!

1095
01:53:34,274 --> 01:53:37,626
I only told you that because
you wanted me to let you go!

1096
01:53:43,149 --> 01:53:44,649
Draw!

1097
01:53:49,622 --> 01:53:51,122
Sir!

1098
01:54:14,681 --> 01:54:16,181
You're very good...

1099
01:54:19,052 --> 01:54:21,169
lf you want to run
now's your chance

1100
01:54:25,291 --> 01:54:26,791
After I kill you

1101
01:54:32,098 --> 01:54:33,598
Draw!

1102
01:54:35,668 --> 01:54:37,491
Sir! There's still time
to stop

1103
01:54:50,016 --> 01:54:51,516
Calm down and think!

1104
01:54:52,619 --> 01:54:54,619
You haven't rested
since yesterday

1105
01:54:56,122 --> 01:54:57,827
You're already breathing hard

1106
01:55:00,860 --> 01:55:02,360
You mock me

1107
01:55:12,305 --> 01:55:14,657
Sir! Continue this
and I'll cut you down

1108
01:55:19,045 --> 01:55:20,545
ls that what you want?

1109
01:55:21,281 --> 01:55:22,781
That's fine by me

1110
01:55:26,653 --> 01:55:28,153
Draw

1111
01:55:58,451 --> 01:55:59,951
You've cut me, Twilight

1112
01:57:11,224 --> 01:57:13,694
This is what you get
for taking me lightly

1113
01:57:46,793 --> 01:57:48,293
Have a seat

1114
01:58:05,278 --> 01:58:06,925
Will you let me go
Twilight?

1115
01:58:13,553 --> 01:58:15,053
That was...

1116
01:58:17,490 --> 01:58:18,990
...my intention

1117
01:58:41,114 --> 01:58:42,614
lt's dark

1118
01:58:50,556 --> 01:58:52,056
I can't see

1119
01:58:59,499 --> 01:59:00,999
Hell

1120
01:59:19,785 --> 01:59:21,285
Twilight...

1121
01:59:55,054 --> 01:59:56,554
ls it over?

1122
02:00:00,960 --> 02:00:02,460
lt's all yours

1123
02:00:08,568 --> 02:00:10,068
Careful!

1124
02:00:16,676 --> 02:00:18,176
He's dead!

1125
02:00:50,176 --> 02:00:51,676
Ito...

1126
02:00:54,146 --> 02:00:55,646
Go buy some tofu

1127
02:00:59,652 --> 02:01:01,152
Don't lose the money

1128
02:01:09,595 --> 02:01:11,095
Miss Kayano!

1129
02:01:11,297 --> 02:01:12,797
lt's the Master!

1130
02:01:24,443 --> 02:01:25,943
Ito...

1131
02:01:28,014 --> 02:01:29,514
...I'm home

1132
02:01:50,102 --> 02:01:51,631
Miss Tomoe! Father's back!

1133
02:02:28,674 --> 02:02:30,174
You're still here...

1134
02:02:40,286 --> 02:02:41,786
Thank heaven!

1135
02:02:44,090 --> 02:02:45,590
I was sure...

1136
02:02:46,792 --> 02:02:48,292
...you were dead!

1137
02:03:01,374 --> 02:03:03,491
Finally Miss Tomoe
became our mother

1138
02:03:07,213 --> 02:03:08,713
My father was happy

1139
02:03:14,053 --> 02:03:17,464
But peace prevailed in our house
for less than three years

1140
02:03:23,262 --> 02:03:25,673
With the Meiji Restoration
came civil war

1141
02:03:27,566 --> 02:03:29,860
Our clan supported
the former Shogun...

1142
02:03:31,404 --> 02:03:34,698
...and fought as rebels
against the emperor's government

1143
02:03:38,577 --> 02:03:40,077
During this 'Boshin War'.

1144
02:03:41,881 --> 02:03:43,763
...my father was shot
and killed

1145
02:04:09,542 --> 02:04:12,836
Tomoe took us, her step-daughters
to Edo, now 'Tokyo'...

1146
02:04:16,615 --> 02:04:19,320
...and supported us
until we were both married

1147
02:04:22,888 --> 02:04:25,711
Now she sleeps with my father
beneath this stone

1148
02:04:31,664 --> 02:04:35,369
ln the new Meiji era, many men
who had worked with my father...

1149
02:04:38,904 --> 02:04:41,198
...rose to positions
of great authority

1150
02:04:44,076 --> 02:04:45,576
I often heard them say...

1151
02:04:47,112 --> 02:04:49,759
...that 'Twilight Seibei
was an unlucky man.'

1152
02:04:51,383 --> 02:04:52,883
But I do not agree

1153
02:04:58,924 --> 02:05:01,688
My father had no desire
to rise in the world...

1154
02:05:04,497 --> 02:05:07,438
...and I don't think
he considered himself unlucky

1155
02:05:10,870 --> 02:05:12,370
He loved his daughters...

1156
02:05:14,473 --> 02:05:16,590
...and the beautiful Tomoe
loved him

1157
02:05:19,044 --> 02:05:21,161
His life, I think
was short but full

1158
02:05:27,253 --> 02:05:29,370
I am proud to have had
such a father

1159
02:05:33,817 --> 02:05:34,317

